# seed once below); every later run lists it. Each candidate below is therefore applied
# after two seed runs, and judged on two runs after it.

== (c) read-only scan of agy.exe (244 091 032 bytes), 1 MB chunks, printable strings within
== 200 bytes of each needle. Counts of strings: swarm 6517, plugins. 1573, enabledPlugins 21,
== disabledPlugins 0. The strings that name a setting:
json:"enabledPlugins"   (in `struct { EnabledPlugins map[string]interface {} }`, the import of another agent's settings)
planner_config.customization_discovery_config.plugins.builtin_plugin_names
plugins.(*Manager).Disable / plugins.(*Manager).Enable / plugins.SetEnabledForDir
"use `plugins.json` to enable specific plugins or inherit them from shared paths"
"`skills.json` or `plugins.json` in your workspace"
"Fixed the agent being blocked from reading your global rules and customization files in
 `~/.gemini/config`, including ... `skills.json`, `rules.json`, `plugins.json`, and `agents.json`"
google3/third_party/jetski/cli/swarm/live/live.enabled
# No swarm-specific setting (no enable_swarm, swarm_enabled or the like) was found.
# The built-in doc builtin/skills/agy-customizations/docs/json_configs.md says skills.json
# and plugins.json in `~/.gemini/config/` take `entries`, `inherits` and a top-level
# `exclude` of patterns matched against directory names.

